                  "theoryContent": "### The Freedom Movement in Andhra and Formation of Andhra State\n\n#### 1. Rampa Rebellion (1922-1924)\n* Led by **Alluri Sitarama Raju** against the oppressive Madras Forest Act of 1882 and Podu cultivation bans.\n* Raju utilized guerrilla warfare tactics, raiding police stations at Chintapalli, Krishnadevipeta, and Rajavommangi.\n\n#### 2. The Linguistic State Struggle\n* **Sri Bagh Pact (15 November 1937):** Agreement between leaders of Coastal Andhra and Rayalaseema assuring balanced university education, irrigation rights (Tungabhadra/Krishna), and choice of capital.\n* **Amarajeevi Potti Sreeramulu:** Fast unto death (58 days) from 19 October 1952 to 15 December 1952 in Madras.\n* Result: **Andhra State inaugurated on 1 October 1953** at Kurnool (first linguistic state in independent India).",
