                  "theoryContent": "### Comprehensive Analysis: Andhra Pradesh Reorganisation Act, 2014\n\nThe bifurcation of erstwhile Andhra Pradesh resulted in severe structural asymmetries: loss of a high-yield revenue generating capital (Hyderabad), lack of Tier-1 industrial clusters, and an initial revenue deficit exceeding ₹16,000 crores.\n\n#### Core Pillars of the Act:\n1. **Section 90 - Polavaram Irrigation Project:**\n   Declared a National Project. The Central Government executes and finances 100% of the remaining irrigation component cost.\n2. **Industrial & Infrastructure Corridors:**\n   * **VCIC (Visakhapatnam-Chennai Industrial Corridor):** Asian Development Bank funded; covers Visakhapatnam, Kakinada, Srikalahasti-Yerpedu nodes.\n   * **CBIC (Chennai-Bengaluru Industrial Corridor):** Includes Krishnapatnam node.",
